PHASE 1 - Database Basics -> CREATE TABLE -> Data Types -> Constraints ->  INSERT -> UPDATE ->  DELETE -> SELECT

Q1 — Identify the concepts

1. A Table is a place where data is stored in a structured way eg - students
2. Row is in the table where we store all the records eg - Rahul, 20, CSE
3. Column is where we specify the which types of data is stored like name, rollno, class eg- name, agee, email
4. id is the primary key
5. database is a collections of tables whereas table is a place where all the data is stored

Q2 -Why would id generally be a better primary key than name?
-because two students can have the same name but not a same id

Q3 id

Q4-
 CREATE TABLE students(
    id INT primary key,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(150) UNIQUE,
    age INT,
    course VARCHAR(50)
);

Q5 CREATE TABLE employees(
    id INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY primary key,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE,
    salary INT CHECK(salary>0),
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

Q6 CREATE TABLE students(
    id INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY primary key,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    age INT CHECK(age>=18),
    email VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
);

Q7-

Data	Type
Student age	- INT
Student name - VARCHAR
Email	- VARCHAR
Date of birth	- DATE
Student's GPA, e.g. 8.75	- DECIMAL
Whether student is active	- Boolean
Exact time a student registered - TIMESTAMPTZ


Q8- 
VARCHAR(100)- variale length limit 
TEXT- unlimited length string

Q9- we use
DECIMAL(6,2)

Q10- 
What constraint would you use for each requirement?

Student must provide a name.- NOT NULL
Every student must have a different email.- UNIQUE
Student age must be at least 18. - CHECK(age>=18)
Every student must have a unique ID. - PRIMARY KEY
A student belongs to an existing department.-

NOT NULL      -> value must exist
UNIQUE        -> values cannot repeat
PRIMARY KEY   -> unique row identifier
CHECK         -> value must satisfy a condition
FOREIGN KEY   -> must reference another table
DEFAULT       -> automatic value when none is provided

Q11- 
     CREATE TABLE users(
        id INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY primary key,
        username VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
        email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE,
        age INT CHECK(age>=18 AND age<=60)        
     );


Q12- CREATE TABLE orders(
    id INT primary key,
    customer_name CHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    amount INT CHECK(amount>0),
    status VARCHAR(100) DEFAULT 'pending',
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);


